# Mechanical Behavior Reference Manifest

This manifest enables Codex to simulate gear systems, torque decay, mechanical failures, and procedural machinery grounded in real-world engineering principles.

---

##  Gear Systems & Rotational Mechanics

**Name:** *MIT Gears and Mechanisms Lecture Notes*  
**Type:** Engineering Course  
**URL:** https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mechanical-engineering/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/unit-i-planar-kinematics/gears/  

**Use:** Details gear ratios, meshing logic, and force propagation. Codex can simulate pulley systems, gear-based gates, or jam-prone rotors.

---

**Name:** *Gear Geometry and Terminology  KHK Gears*  
**Type:** Industry Whitepaper  
**URL:** https://khkgears.net/new/gear_knowledge/gear_technical_reference.html  

**Use:** Defines pitch, backlash, stress curves, gear tooth failure. Codex may apply this to destructible gearboxes or entropy-driven collapse points.

---

##  Torque, Load & Mechanical Fatigue

**Name:** *Torque and Power Transmission  Machine Design Handbook*  
**Type:** Engineering Manual  
**URL:** https://www.engineersedge.com/calculators/mechanical-power.htm  

**Use:** Defines torque decay under load. Codex may simulate strain-based slowdown, momentum stutter, or snapping thresholds.

---

**Name:** *Mechanical Fatigue  Fatigue Failure Theories*  
**Type:** Engineering Analysis  
**URL:** https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/mechanical-fatigue  

**Use:** Stress cycle breakdown, microfracture buildup. Codex can use this to build entropy-weighted gear lifespan or decay triggers.

---

##  Procedural Assembly & Breakdown

**Name:** *Linkages & Mechanisms Library  507 Mechanical Movements*  
**Type:** Historical Engineering Archive  
**URL:** https://507movements.com/  

**Use:** Massive bank of working mechanical systems. Codex may generate siege devices, puzzle locks, or machine NPCs using modular link logic.

